        "text": "You can also short the market. In swing trading, this means borrowing overpriced assets and then repurchasing them at a lower price. For example, Bob's analysis predicts that Ether's price will drop from 2000 to 1000 in two weeks. Bob borrows one Ether, sells it for 2000 today, and waits to see if his prediction is correct. Two weeks later, Ether has dropped down to $1,500. Although he wasn't 100% accurate with his analysis, Bob still has the opportunity to make some profit. Bob repurchases back one ether for $1,500 and returns the ether back to the lender, leaving him with $500 in profit. Swing traders commonly use technical analysis like day trading. But as their strategy plays out across a more extended period, fundamental analysis is also a valuable tool for swing traders. Using them both together can create an even more robust analysis to base your trades on.",
        "start": 240,
        "end": 56090,
        "confidence": 0.985935,
